1
00:00:00,929 --> 00:00:03,019
This is Habit-to-Value Studio,

2
00:00:03,019 --> 00:00:07,058
an independent concept by Ayo Ahmed for the Bending Spoons

3
00:00:07,058 --> 00:00:10,053
Growth manager role. All data is synthetic.

4
00:00:10,053 --> 00:00:13,745
It is not affiliated with Evernote or Bending Spoons.

5
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:18,013
In the task-first journey, a new user picks a job first:

6
00:00:18,013 --> 00:00:20,537
turn meeting notes into next actions.

7
00:00:20,537 --> 00:00:23,674
That opens an original synthetic meeting note.

8
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:28,965
The note is editable. I change the title and save it locally.

9
00:00:28,965 --> 00:00:31,108
Nothing leaves the browser.

10
00:00:31,559 --> 00:00:35,627
Now I tick the lines that need doing and turn them into

11
00:00:35,627 --> 00:00:37,993
tasks. The note stays unchanged,

12
00:00:37,993 --> 00:00:40,730
and each task links back to its line.

13
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:42,431
First value is reached.

14
00:00:42,882 --> 00:00:46,504
I schedule a revisit for day two and simulate it.

15
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:50,496
No notification is sent. The cue names the open tasks.

16
00:00:50,496 --> 00:00:54,414
Completing one on a later day counts as repeat value.

17
00:00:54,414 --> 00:00:58,036
Only then does a transparent plan preview appear,

18
00:00:58,036 --> 00:01:00,402
and it never purchases anything.

19
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:04,935
Now the growth side. I import a seeded cohort CSV.

20
00:01:04,935 --> 00:01:07,874
Rows are validated and deduplicated,

21
00:01:07,874 --> 00:01:11,221
and users come only from assignment rows.

22
00:01:11,671 --> 00:01:14,751
The contract is pre-registered before results:

23
00:01:14,751 --> 00:01:16,693
user-level stable assignment,

24
00:01:16,693 --> 00:01:18,835
intent-to-treat, mature windows,

25
00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:20,911
minimum sample, and guardrails.

26
00:01:21,362 --> 00:01:25,552
This cohort shows a six point lift in repeat value overall.

27
00:01:25,552 --> 00:01:29,032
But traffic mix differed between the ramp phases.

28
00:01:29,032 --> 00:01:31,447
Holding the acquisition mix fixed,

29
00:01:31,447 --> 00:01:34,287
the effect reverses to minus two points.

30
00:01:34,287 --> 00:01:36,986
So the decision is iterate, not scale.

31
00:01:37,437 --> 00:01:41,899
Next, conversion goes up, but refunds rise and repeat

32
00:01:41,899 --> 00:01:46,024
value falls. Net revenue per eligible user drops.

33
00:01:46,024 --> 00:01:48,045
The rollout is rejected.

34
00:01:48,495 --> 00:01:51,177
Finally, a biased, incomplete export.

35
00:01:51,177 --> 00:01:54,874
Refund events are missing, assignments are dropped,

36
00:01:54,874 --> 00:01:58,715
the sample ratio is off, and most users are immature.

37
00:01:58,715 --> 00:02:02,847
The tool refuses to call a winner and lists every reason.

38
00:02:03,297 --> 00:02:07,221
Every analysis exports an evidence memo with the contract,

39
00:02:07,221 --> 00:02:09,994
gates, results, decision and limitations.

40
00:02:09,994 --> 00:02:11,956
That's Habit-to-Value Studio:

41
00:02:11,956 --> 00:02:15,609
a working user flow, and a disciplined scale decision.
